		text = "A Nest is the walled heart of a District, run and protected by its Wing. Some Nest walls are electric fences or walls of light. Some are a couple of loose chains. It doesn't matter: Backstreets people don't cross without papers, and the papers cost money.\n\nInside, the streets are clean, the drones are always watching, and the rules are strict. Nest residence has to be paid for every year, and it can be refused. A bad record, unpaid taxes, or simply having fought in the Smoke War can keep you outside for good.\n\nNest windows look out over the Backstreets, and the Backstreets look back. Some Nest families sit by the glass in the evening and watch the streets below like a show.",
