		title = "The Rules of the Night",
		text = "From 3:13 until the third wave has passed, the City shuts its eyes. During the Night in the Backstreets it is a City Taboo to record video or sound, and a City Taboo to break into or destroy someone else's home. A City Taboo comes from the Head itself, and breaking one is about the worst thing a person can do. The Head's Claws do not hold trials.\n\nThe second rule is why a locked home is the safest place in the City. Even the Fingers won't touch a home during the Night. Out on the street it's the opposite: nothing is forbidden, nothing is recorded, and in the morning there is nothing left to find.\n\nSo every Backstreets child learns it before they can count: be home before three, lock the door, and stay away from the window.",
