		secret = true,
		text = "People who have seen them up close describe a crowd: people, maybe, rusty and slow-voiced, far too many to count, moving like water. They rise out of the ground along the edge of every Nest and march through the Backstreets to the far side for eighty minutes, in three waves, with about ten minutes of quiet between.\n\nThey talk, in pieces, as if every word had to be fetched from somewhere far away. Anything left on the street is cleaning to them: rubbish, bodies, illegal buildings, people. Strike one down and the others step around it and keep walking. The only ones they pass by are the ones strong enough to stand their ground.\n\nNobody knows what they are. Old Fixers say the Head wields them. Nobody has ever asked the Head.",
