		text = "Rats are the bottom rung of Backstreets crime: small packs of muggers and thieves with no Syndicate behind them. Nobody survives alone in the Backstreets, so Rats move in packs and pick on anyone who looks like they're on their own.\n\nMost Rats have the same dream: to be noticed by a real Syndicate and get in. Very few make it. The rest get swept up by Fixers, by bigger gangs, or by the Night.\n\nEveryone looks down on Rats. Plenty of people started out as one. Nobody keeps score of them, either: there's no boss to answer to, no name to avenge, and when one of them doesn't come back, nobody asks where he went.",
