		text = "An examinee town is a stretch of the Backstreets full of cheap rooms, cram schools and very tired young people, all studying for the same thing: a Wing's entrance exam. Pass, and you become a Feather, with a badge, a salary and maybe a way into the Nest. Fail, and you study for next year.\n\nThe Wing exams test the mind, the way the Hana Association's Fixer license tests the body. Families save for years to send one child to an examinee town. Rats laugh at the examinees. Some of those Rats used to be examinees.",
